{"qid":"Q187830","names":["Second Republic of Austria"],"title":"Second Republic of Austria","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Second Republic of Austria was proclaimed on 27 April 1945 as Soviet forces entered Vienna, re-establishing the democratic constitution of 1920 after the annexation by Nazi Germany (Anschluss) in 1938. Occupied jointly by the four Allied powers until the Austrian State Treaty of 15 May 1955, Austria then regained full sovereignty and declared permanent neutrality, enabling it to serve as a Cold War meeting ground and host to major international organizations including the IAEA and OPEC. Austria joined the European Union in 1995 and remains a federal parliamentary republic, continuing to the present.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The territorial extent of the Second Republic is precisely delineated by the 1955 State Treaty and is not in dispute.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: History of Austria","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Austria"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Austrian State Treaty","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Austrian_State_Treaty"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Second Austrian Republic","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Austrian_Republic"}],"britannica":"topic/history-of-Austria","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"History of Austria","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Karl Renner","nativeName":"Karl Renner","roman":"Karl Renner","start":1945,"end":1950,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Theodor Körner","nativeName":"Theodor Körner","roman":"Theodor Korner","start":1951,"end":1957,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLic